  "text": {
    "intro": "The Thistledown Ascent is less a race than a slow argument conducted at two thousand feet.\nFive pilots are involved. Determine each pilot's start time, landing site and ballast.\n- **Pilot**: Isolde, Anneliese, Rosalind, Grover and Horatio.\n- **Start time** (listed from earlier to later): 8am, 9am, 10am, 11am and noon.\n- **Landed at**: a cricket pitch, a cabbage field, a golf course bunker, a reservoir bank and a caravan park.\n- **Ballast**: pea gravel, dried beans, lead shot, iron filings and sandbags.\nEvery pilot has a different start time, landing site and ballast, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "Rosalind comes down in a golf course bunker. The pilot who comes down in a caravan park falls somewhere between Grover and Rosalind in start time order.",
      "The pilot who carries iron filings is earlier than noon in start time order.",
      "Isolde does not launch at 9am.",
      "The pilot who carries dried beans and noon are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The pilot who comes down in a cabbage field is later than 10am in start time order.",
      "The pilot who carries pea gravel does not come down in a reservoir bank.",
      "The pilot who carries iron filings and Horatio are exactly two hours apart in start time order. Grover is earlier than the pilot who carries iron filings in start time order.",
      "The pilot who carries lead shot and Horatio are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The pilot who carries sandbags falls somewhere between the pilot who comes down in a caravan park and the pilot who comes down in a golf course bunker in start time order."
